      "content": "\"biotic acoustic design\"?? i've never even heard of that term being used in a way that implies surveillance. the way you said it makes it sound like there's a specific way they're engineered to work for this. \n\nif the city or the library board actually implemented this, how would they hide the actual sensors? like, would they be embedded in the soil or maybe integrated into the leaf structure itself so they don't look like anything more than a regular plant? give me an idea of how that would even function technically.",
